          "target": {
            "kind": "by_canonical_key",
            "template": "fiber:package:{definition.name}"
          },
          "attributes": {}
        }
      ],
      "evidence_class": "observed",
      "confidence": "exact",
      "coverage_note": "Which files are Fiber files and which part of the Fiber stack each pulls in -- the router, a middleware under .../middleware/*, a storage driver, a template engine, a contrib package. This is the only fact that says a Go file is a Fiber file at all; every other rule here is gated on it."
    },
