  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "app.Add(verb, url, handler) puts the URL in call.arg1, which omega-go publishes with its quote bytes; a canonical key template has no strip, so an Add route is keyed by its registration site and not by the URL it serves. Every other verb is keyed by its URL.",
      "omega-go emits no definition for a short variable declaration, so `api := app.Group(prefix)` never binds the name api to that prefix. call.method now publishes the receiver, so api.Get and app.Get are distinguishable as text, but a route registered on a group is still keyed by its own path with the group prefix not prepended, and the group's routes are not nested under it.",
      "An aliased router import -- f \"github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2\" -- makes the constructor read f.New(), which fiber.app.construct does not recognise; every other rule is gated on the import path and is unaffected.",
      "runtime route state: routes built in a loop, handlers held in a slice or a map, and anything registered through reflection are outside static scope."
    ]
  },
